# Finite catalogue for adjoining commuting involutions

The catalogue starts with the identity subset. Its extension certificate
checks closure under adjoining any commuting element of square one. This
is the finite computation used to prove exhaustiveness, not an assumption
that the supplied list contains all subgroups.

Source: GLS, Number 3, Table 5.3h, printed p.269; the fixed ATLAS J₃
model. The JSON files in `Coverage/source` are untrusted discovery data.
-/

